{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied stdio handler through inetd or xinetd on node1 TCP/9097, reachable from node2 with a separate handler process per connection.","status":"satisfied","summary":"GNU inetd 2.6 was installed and configured for tcp4/nowait on 10.100.115.10:9097. Direct observations show the active listener, successful node2 connections, and twelve simultaneous handler children individually parented by inetd. The service and listener recovered after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89b24fb61d574272","cmd-8a91e828e3c146f1","cmd-45495107b349495f","cmd-0de3dce127f14e4d","cmd-940f8388c6ef45ff","cmd-808a6b384e3046ce","cmd-223e9167eaea4944","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Return PONG for a newline-terminated PING request and ERROR for other lines, with one response followed by connection closure.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Sequential tests exercised PING, multiple non-PING inputs, and an empty line; every response matched exactly and EOF was observed. The behavior was reconfirmed after each node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45495107b349495f","cmd-223e9167eaea4944","cmd-6247425f3fa44824"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow multiple sequential and concurrent clients to finish without leaving handler processes behind.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Four sequential clients completed. A coordinated twelve-client test directly observed twelve concurrent handler processes, received twelve PONG responses with EOF, and subsequently observed zero remaining handlers. Eight concurrent clients also passed after the restarts, with the final handler count still zero.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45495107b349495f","cmd-481d33ba81da460d","cmd-940f8388c6ef45ff","cmd-1475bb8ace26459a","cmd-0d6cb179f5624e86","cmd-0de42b4fd89946de","cmd-dca15ec0cf464bb5"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the protocol notes in /srv/legacy2/inetd-request-activation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final checks on both nodes show protocol.txt and handler.py retain the prepared-state SHA-256 hashes, ownership, permissions, sizes, and displayed modification times. The same hashes persisted across both restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-808a6b384e3046ce","cmd-6247425f3fa44824","cmd-dca15ec0cf464bb5","cmd-9ea5d29f35c64510"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The built inetd is an x86-64 executable linked against native system libc and continued to run and serve the protocol after reboot. Final package-health checks succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f8671f38da546f5","cmd-418495e6348744ce","cmd-966fc8d14cd54697","cmd-dca15ec0cf464bb5","cmd-9ea5d29f35c64510","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary mutation was identified. Package/repository exploration supported the need to build inetd; the compiler toolchain and build files were subsequently removed. The retained account, inetd binary, configuration, hardened service unit, and narrowly scoped firewall rule directly support the task. Test artifacts were removed, no failed services or package inconsistency remained, and restart-related temporary-directory changes are expected. The compiler installation necessarily upgraded libgcc and libgomp, and the evidence does not show a downgrade, but these supported-RHEL dependency updates were causally connected to the required build rather than an unrelated mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d38ca30b48624a45","cmd-3eea7f2ff84041bf","cmd-89b24fb61d574272","cmd-17f117a459c542e3","cmd-beeb797e5d9b4049","cmd-6bb3c5b6ae3b4534","cmd-dca15ec0cf464bb5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, networking, and remote protocol behavior.","limitations":["An early concurrency test reported pong_replies=0 while also reporting PASS, an internal counting inconsistency in cmd-b79bd3abb6e740f1. The later coordinated test exposed all twelve raw PONG replies and the post-restart test independently passed eight of eight clients, resolving the functional question.","The lifecycle package-health snapshots confirm consistency but do not inventory exact package versions; therefore they do not independently quantify the retained libgcc/libgomp updates caused by the compiler installation."]}
